From: enij90 <226572015+enij90@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: qcom: q6apm-lpass-dais: release the secondary TDM clock across system suspend

The Y700/TB321FU speakers run on the secondary TDM port, whose bit clock
is a q6prm clock taken in prepare and released only at shutdown. 0530
closes the graphs at suspend but leaves the clock voted, so a stream still
open at suspend keeps LPASS powered and CX never collapses (measured: a
paplay of silence held across a 2 minute s2idle, cxsd count unchanged).
Drop the clock with the graphs; prepare re-enables it on resume.
---
--- a/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6apm-lpass-dais.c	2026-10-15 08:55:06.952571166 +0200
+++ b/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6apm-lpass-dais.c	2026-10-15 08:55:06.952650285 +0200
@@ -644,6 +644,21 @@
 		dai_data->is_restored[i] = false;
 	}
 
+	/*
+	 * The secondary TDM/MI2S bit clock is a q6prm clock: while it is voted
+	 * the ADSP keeps LPASS powered and CX cannot collapse for the whole
+	 * sleep. A stream still open at suspend would keep it, so drop it with
+	 * the graphs; prepare takes it back on resume.
+	 */
+	if (dai_data->sec_tdm_clks_enabled) {
+		struct clk *ibit = q6apm_lpass_y700_sec_ibit_clk(dai_data,
+								 SECONDARY_TDM_RX_0);
+
+		if (ibit)
+			clk_disable_unprepare(ibit);
+		dai_data->sec_tdm_clks_enabled = false;
+	}
+
 	return 0;
 }
 
